{"name":"Athena","hex":"#dcd7cc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Athena","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The goddess of wisdom, especially strategic warfare, the arts, and especially crafts, in particular, weaving; daughter of Zeus and Metis. Her Roman counterpart is Minerva.","A city in Umatilla County, Oregon, United States."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman who colludes with the patriarchy rather than actively opposing it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Athena"}],"entries":[{"title":"Athena","blocks":[{"text":"Athena or Athene, often given the epithet Pallas, is an ancient Greek goddess associated with wisdom, warfare, and handicraft who was later syncretised with the Roman goddess Minerva and Etruscan Menrva. Athena was regarded as the patron and protectress of various cities across Greece, particularly the city of Athens, from which she most likely received her name. Her major symbols include owls, olive trees, snakes, and the gorgoneion. In art, she is generally depicted wearing a helmet and holding a spear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Mattei_Athena_Louvre_Ma530_n2.jpg/330px-Mattei_Athena_Louvre_Ma530_n2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athena","wikidata":"Q37122"},{"title":"Athena (wrestler)","blocks":[{"text":"Adrienne Palmer is an American professional wrestler. She is signed to All Elite Wrestling (AEW), where she performs under the ring name Athena. She primarily appears in AEW's sister promotion Ring of Honor (ROH), where she is the leader of the M.I.T stable and the current ROH Women's World Champion in her first reign; at 1401 days, she is the longest-reigning champion in ROH history. She also makes appearances on the independent circuit and is the co-owner of Metroplex Wrestling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Athena_-_August_29_2025_%28cropped1%29.jpg/330px-Athena_-_August_29_2025_%28cropped1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athena_(wrestler)","wikidata":"Q21107056"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Akropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg/500px-Akropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Akropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg/1280px-Akropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Akropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg/500px-Akropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Acropolis at Athens (1846) by Leo von Klenze.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkropolis_by_Leo_von_Klenze.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/91/Goddess-boars-tusk-griffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/91/Goddess-boars-tusk-griffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Fragment of a fresco from the Cult Center at Mycenae dating the late thirteenth century BC depicting a warrior goddess, possibly Athena, wearing a boar's tusk helmet and clutching a griffin.[12]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoddess-boars-tusk-griffin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Seal_of_Inanna%2C_2350-2150_BCE.jpg/500px-Seal_of_Inanna%2C_2350-2150_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Seal_of_Inanna%2C_2350-2150_BCE.jpg/1280px-Seal_of_Inanna%2C_2350-2150_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.